{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/commands/land-check.ts","codegenInstructions":"Verify each finding against current code. Fix only still-valid issues, skip the rest with a brief reason, keep changes minimal, and validate.\n\nIn @src/commands/land-check.ts around lines 947 - 969, hasOpenNoReviewerGap currently uses find(...) and can incorrectly treat a ledger as resolved when duplicate entries exist; change it to consider all ledger.gaps with id \"BANDIT-GAP-NO-REVIEWER-CONFIGURED\" by using filter/findAll semantics and evaluate their statuses collectively: if no matching gaps fall back to declaredGapIds.includes(targetId) as before; if there are matching gaps, return true (open) if any matching gap has a non-terminal status (i.e., not \"resolved\" and not \"replaced\"); only return false when all matching gaps are terminal. Update the logic inside hasOpenNoReviewerGap to iterate over ledger.gaps (using Array.prototype.filter or equivalent) and compute the final boolean accordingly.","suggestions":[]}
{"type":"finding","severity":"major","fileName":"src/commands/init.ts","codegenInstructions":"","suggestions":[],"comment":"**Profile template is now incompatible with the new typed reviewer validator.**\n\n`validateTypedProfileReviewers` now requires `reviewers[i].type` (and type-specific adapter fields), but the built-in `PROJECT_PROFILE_TEMPLATE` example still emits untyped reviewer entries. A user following the generated template will now fail `init --profile` by default.\n\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  \"reviewers\": [\n-    { \"id\": \"local-qwen-baseline\", \"provider\": \"local_qwen\", \"required\": true }\n-  ],\n+  \"reviewers\": [\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"local-qwen-baseline\",\n+      \"type\": \"openai_compatible\",\n+      \"provider\": \"local_qwen\",\n+      \"required\": true,\n+      \"provider_base_url\": \"http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n```\n</details>\n\nAs per coding guidelines, request changes for “parser/writer mismatch”."}
